BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Ride Why
DTSTART:20250630T023000Z
DTEND:20250630T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20250630T023000Z
UID:eCvxvJ1WdE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nPresented by Noir Rouge Producti
 ons. We Ride Why is a documentary film about the power of love\, community
 \, and hope in the face of cancer. The film follows the stories of several
  women who have been impacted by cancer\, as well as the friends and famil
 y who support them. Through their stories\, we learn about the collateral 
 damage that cancer can bring\, but also the hope that can be found in the 
 relationships that are born out of trauma. We also see how a strong commu
 nity in Seattle\, Washington has formed to support all those impacted by c
 ancer.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/we-ride-why
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:1999: The Year That Changed Everything
DTSTART:20250701T010000Z
DTEND:20250701T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250701T010000Z
UID:c2rnP6Jwyn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nWhat made 1999 stand out as a yea
 r of bold\, boundary-pushing films that still resonate today? Join local f
 ilmmaker and television producer Jeremy Cropf in this special SIFF Member 
 Talk as he unpacks the unique cultural\, industrial\, and technological fo
 rces that reshaped Hollywood’s creative landscape. While the spotlight w
 ill be on Hollywood and American indie films\, we’ll also take time to a
 ppreciate notable international films to provide rich context and contrast
 . To reserve your free member tickets\, click the "SIGN IN" button in the 
 upper corner of this screen. Once signed in\, click the showtime below to 
 reserve your tickets.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/educatio
 n/adult-film-education/film-talks/members-only-1999-film-talk
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art for Everybody
DTSTART:20250704T020000Z
DTEND:20250704T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20250704T020000Z
UID:Rmam4jd1P0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nThomas Kinkade was one of the mos
 t successful artists of his day\, with millions of cozy cottage paintings 
 sold across the U.S. On his passing in 2012\, a newly discovered vault con
 tained a series of darkly themed paintings that reveal a more complicated 
 and troubled man than his most popular works implied.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/cinema/in-theaters/art-for-everybody
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
